---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONFIG } from '../../config.js';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy — SINAPTIA"
  description="What the Sinaptia site processes, where it lives, and how to delete it."
  lang="en"
>
  <main class="wrap wrap-narrow" style="padding:64px 26px">
    <div class="eyebrow"><i></i> privacy</div>
    <h1 class="sec-title">What we know about you, and what we do not</h1>
    <p class="sec-lead">Short version: no advertising cookies, no pixels. What exists is what you choose to type or say.</p>

    <h3 style="margin:26px 0 8px">1 · Your browser</h3>
    <p>The agent talks, stores the conversation and generates your brief inside your browser. The
      PDF stays on your device. You can clear the site data at any time from your browser settings.</p>

    <h3 style="margin:26px 0 8px">2 · Temporary conversation memory</h3>
    <p>So Nexa does not lose the thread when you reload or lock your phone, the conversation is kept
      in this browser's local storage for up to 12 hours after the last turn. It is not shared across
      devices. Type “start over” in the chat to delete it immediately. After 12 hours it is removed
      automatically.</p>

    <h3 style="margin:26px 0 8px">3 · The AI provider</h3>
    <p>When you talk to Nexa, your message and the conversation context are sent to the configured
      model provider (Groq by default) to generate the reply. We do not use that data to train our
      own models or third-party models. Provider keys live on the server, never in your browser. If
      you prefer not to send anything to a model, the local engine still answers without a network.</p>

    <h3 style="margin:26px 0 8px">4 · Voice</h3>
    <p>Speech recognition uses your browser's native capability. In desktop Chrome the audio is
      processed by Google's speech service (not our integration, but not fully local either); in Safari
      it is processed locally. The microphone only turns on after you tap. The video-call interpreter
      does not record or store audio.</p>

    <h3 style="margin:26px 0 8px">5 · A copy of your brief</h3>
    <p>Your PDF is downloaded to your device. We also try to send a copy to the Sinaptia team so we can
      reply; if no delivery channel is configured, the site offers you Share or Email instead. The copy
      contains the details you gave in the conversation and the proposed project.</p>

    <h3 style="margin:26px 0 8px">6 · Your rights</h3>
    <p>Access, correction, deletion, portability and objection. Message us on
      <a href={CONFIG.marca.whatsappUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">WhatsApp {CONFIG.marca.whatsapp}</a> and we
      will handle it without asking for more data than needed to identify you.</p>

    <p style="margin-top:30px"><a href="/en/">← Back to Sinaptia</a> · <a href="/privacidad/">Versión en español</a></p>
  </main>
</Base>
